    "note": "As filed. Title says mental health, but the only operative part amends the firearm permit law."
  },
  "operative_text": "SECTION 1 (HRS 134-2(c)): An applicant for a permit shall sign a waiver at the time of application, allowing the chief of police of the county issuing the permit access to any records that have a bearing on the mental health of the applicant. Prior to the issuance of any permit, the chief of police of the county issuing the permit shall attest that a review of any records pertaining to the applicant's mental health, including but not limited to any records relating to court mandated treatment for anger management or domestic violence counseling, has been completed."
